# Phase 7 Architecture Validation

The failure tests validated the following chain:

```text
              Failure
                 │
                 ▼
        Kubernetes detects
             failure
                 │
                 ▼
       ┌─────────────────┐
       │ Reconciliation  │
       │    Controller   │
       └────────┬────────┘
                │
                ▼
       Replacement Pod
                │
                ▼
       Application Recovery
```

For PostgreSQL:

```text
PostgreSQL Pod Failure
        │
        ▼
Pod recreated
        │
        ▼
PersistentVolume checked
        │
        ▼
local-path node affinity
        │
        ▼
Cross-node scheduling blocked
```

This exposed the storage dependency of the current architecture.

---

# Phase 7 Final Result

Phase 7 successfully validated the resilience of the private-cloud Data Warehouse infrastructure.

The tests demonstrated:

* Kubernetes self-healing
* Pod recovery
* Worker node maintenance behavior
* Monitoring recovery
* Database integrity
* PostgreSQL health monitoring
* Persistent storage limitations
* Real-world failure behavior

### Phase 7 Status

**COMPLETE ✅**

### Overall Finding

The private cloud successfully handles application and monitoring failures through Kubernetes reconciliation.

However, PostgreSQL currently depends on node-local persistent storage, meaning database failover across worker nodes is not yet fully highly available.

This limitation has been identified and documented as a future architectural improvement.

